{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789465828,"nonce":"C7+1GFzkmckWLO3/v0cFi+oapWc=","title":"HIR to CLIF translation costs about 5 us per instruction","message":"`compile_function_body` took 3.6 ms to translate a 680-instruction function while Cranelift's own `define_function` on the result took 2.4 ms; per function the eager module compile averages 0.15 to 0.25 ms where Ash's AIR to CLIF lowering is at 0.04 ms. Compile time on the Python kernels is 30 ms of codegen for the library, and every promotion and first-call compile pays the same rate while holding the backend lock.\n\nProfile the translation on a large function (records' or tokenize's `main`, 2000 instructions) and fix what the profile names. Candidates from reading: per-value type caches rebuilt per function, `osr_layout` per loop header at tier 0, `HashMap\u003cHirId, _\u003e` lookups with SipHash on every operand (the HirId maps elsewhere moved to a cheaper hasher), string formatting of names on the hot path.","files":null}]}